## Validation & Quality Rules

Before marking any changes as complete, you must always execute the following workflow from the root directory:
1. Run `npm run clean` : This command will clean up the development environment.
2. Run `npm run fix` : This command will automatically fix any formatting issues in the **Template Development Environment**.
3. Run `npm run test` : This command will run the test suite to ensure that all tests pass successfully.

## Commit Message Rules

You must strictly follow the Conventional Commits (v1.0.0) specification for all Git commit messages. Structure your commit messages as follows:
`<type>[optional scope]: <description>`

Allowed types include:
- `feat`: A new feature (correlates with MINOR versioning).
- `fix`: A bug fix (correlates with PATCH versioning).
- `docs`, `style`, `refactor`, `perf`, `test`, `chore`, `build`, `ci`.

*Note: For breaking changes, append a `!` after the type/scope or include `BREAKING CHANGE:` in the footer (correlates with MAJOR versioning).*
